// John — ICT Engine
// Built module by module from the ICT 2016/2017 Core Content and the 2022 Mentorship.
// Detection rules are specified in "John — ICT Concept Detection Spec" (Part numbers referenced below).
// Generated from John/src/ by John/build.py: edit the module files there, not this file.
//
// Top-down by design: market structure is read only from Daily, H4, H1 and M15 candles, whatever the
// chart's timeframe, so a level means the same thing on every chart. A chart shows the structure of its
// own timeframe and every higher one: an M1 chart shows all four, an H4 chart shows H4 and Daily.
// M1/M5 candles never decide structure, and raids vs runs are always judged on M15 candles.
//
// Modules in this file:
//   Market structure · ITH/ITL and LTH/LTL on D, H4, H1, M15 (Spec Part 2.1–2.2)
//   Liquidity map    · BSL/SSL pools, equal highs/lows, raid vs run (Spec Part 3.1–3.3)
//   Time map         · midnight separators, day names, killzone boxes (Spec Part 1.2–1.3, 5.1)
//   Power of 3       · accumulation, manipulation (Judas swing) and distribution boxes (Spec Part 5.3)
//   PD arrays        · FVGs and order blocks on D, H4, H1, M15: draws on liquidity, not entries (Spec Part 2.3–2.4, 4)
//   Setups           · raid of liquidity → market structure shift on M1/M3/M5 → entry at the M1/M3/M5 FVG
//                      (or order block), stop beyond the peak, target the next untaken liquidity
//
// Switched off for now (kept in John/src/disabled/, not built): Daily bias, IPDA 20/40/60 ranges.

//@version=6
indicator("John — ICT Engine", shorttitle = "John", overlay = true, max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500)

